  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "**This is the easy version of the problem. Here, you only need to output the minimum cost only.**\n\nYou are given 222 binary strings AAA and BBB, both of length NNN.\n\nYou can perform the following operation on AAA multiple times (possibly 000):\n\n\nChoose LLL and RRR such that 1≤L≤R≤N1 \\le L \\le R \\le N1≤L≤R≤N, and flip all the values AL,AL+1,…,ARA_L, A_{L + 1}, \\ldots, A_RAL​,AL+1​,…,AR​.\nThe cost of this operation is 111 if AL=ARA_L = A_RAL​=AR​, and 000 otherwise.\nFlipping a value means changing it to a 111 if it was 000, and vice versa.\n\nWhat is the minimum total cost of operations to transform AAA to BBB.\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line of input will contain a single integer TTT, denoting the number of test cases.\nEach test case consists of multiple lines of input.\n\nThe first line contains a single integer NNN.\nThe second line contains a binary string AAA.\nThe third line contains a binary string BBB.\n\n\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each test case, output the minimum total cost of transforming AAA to BBB.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤1001 \\le T \\le 1001≤T≤100",
      "1≤N≤501 \\le N \\le 501≤N≤50",
      "∣A∣=∣B∣=N|A| = |B| = N∣A∣=∣B∣=N",
      "Ai∈{0,1}A_i \\in \\{0, 1\\}Ai​∈{0,1}",
      "Bi∈{0,1}B_i \\in \\{0, 1\\}Bi​∈{0,1}"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "",
    "outputFormat": "",
    "notes": [],
    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "4\n3\n010\n110\n2\n00\n11\n1\n0\n0\n3\n010\n111",
        "output": "0\n1\n0\n1",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nTest Case 1: First, we do the operation on L=2L = 2L=2 and R=3R = 3R=3 to get A=001A = 001A=001, and then on L=1L = 1L=1 and R=3R = 3R=3 to get A=110A = 110A=110. This makes AAA equal to BBB for 000 cost."
      }
    ]
  },
